WATCHDOG
--------

Watchdog is designed to allow password protection on the Psion S3 (or
S3a) that is less "Annoying" than the system password.  It is 2 OPL
programs, WATCHDOG.OPO and SYS$PSWD.OPO.  Watchdog controls SYS$PSWD
and allows setting of options, password etc.  This is an outline of
what it does.

Watchdog handles possible "OFF" events, currently 2 timeout or
Psion+1, it logs the time that the Psion was switched off and when the
Psion is switched on checks against the "Time" setting.  If the time
switched off is greater than set it requests the user defined
password, not allowing access to the Psion until it is entered.  If
the time is less than the "Time" setting then Watchdog transparently
allows use of the Psion.

